  "description": "NINKUS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H172 Gd8 N16 O40,6(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.754-3.925 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.33-115.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd8(LH2)4(μ-Piv)4(η2-Piv)4(μ-OMe)4]·6CH3OH·2H2O.",
